UID:63f70690497b3c65fded8d88f55b70c928ff36f4@wtw-cinemas
DTSTAMP:20260901T142359Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261028
SUMMARY:Manon - Royal Ballet & Opera 26-27 Season @ WTW St Austell
DESCRIPTION:Manon - Royal Ballet & Opera 26-27 Season (3h 10min)\n\nIn the 
 seedy underbelly of 18th-century Paris\, money is king. Nothing is sacred 
 – even love itself can be bought for the right price. A native of this hed
 onistic underworld\, Manon is caught between twin desires when she falls i
 n love with the student Des Grieux. Steadfast and devoted\, he offers the 
 possibility of an honourable life. Yet\, the riches promised by the world 
 of Parisian society remain tempting...\nManon's inner turmoil and struggl
 e for survival lie at the devastating heart of Kenneth MacMillan's 1974 ad
 aptation of Abbé Prévost's novel. In this signature work of The Royal Ball
 et\, MacMillan's nuanced understanding of human psychology makes for an un
 flinching look into the moral degradation of Manon's Paris\, while all its
  decadence and decay are brought to life through Jules Massenet's score an
 d Nicholas Georgiadis's designs.\n\nFilm release at WTW Cinemas St Austell
 \nBook tickets: https://wtwcinemas.co.uk/st-austell/film/5556/manon-royal-
 ballet-opera-2627-season\n\nFilm details: https://evenwebb.github.io/wtw-c
 inemas/films/manon-royal-ballet-opera-26-27-season.html
LOCATION:WTW Cinemas St Austell
URL:https://wtwcinemas.co.uk/st-austell/film/5556/manon-royal-ballet-opera-
 2627-season
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2a51ca19a83af56c9064a422c4e86eed70ec83be@wtw-cinemas
DTSTAMP:20260901T142359Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261105
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261106
SUMMARY:National Theatre Live: Golden Boy @ WTW St Austell
DESCRIPTION:National Theatre Live: Golden Boy (3h)\nDrama\n\n1930s New York
 \, at the height of the Depression. Joe Bonaparte is a gifted young violin
 ist with extraordinary talent and a future in music\, until a chance at fa
 me and fortune lures him into the brutal world of professional boxing. Pre
 ssured by a ruthless manager\, tempted by a forbidden love\, and bound by 
 the expectations of his Italian-American family\, Joe is a young man torn 
 between the seductive promise of the American Dream and the quiet honor of
  a decent life. He must confront what he’s willing to sacrifice\, who he’s
  willing to become\, and how to find his place in a world that demands he 
 choose a side. Sam Yates directs Josh O'Connor in this searing revival of 
 Clifford Odets' knockout American classic. Brought to life with a live str
 ing quartet\, this propulsive drama explores ambition\, identity\, and the
